# URLs lychee skips in the monthly link check (.github/workflows/links.yml), one regular
# expression per line. Only sites that refuse automated requests but whose pages exist go here:
# each was seen refusing lychee, and its page confirmed through another service, on the date
# given. Everything else that fails is reported, so a dead page is not hidden here.

# DOIs. scripts/links/monthly.mjs checks that each one redirects at doi.org; the publisher
# pages behind them often answer 403 to automated requests (ACS, Wiley, ACM; 2026-11-03).
^https?://(dx\.)?doi\.org/

# LinkedIn answers 999 to automated requests (2026-11-03).
^https?://([a-z]+\.)?linkedin\.com/

# Publishers and newspapers that answered lychee 403; each page confirmed to exist, 2026-11-03.
^https?://journals\.biologists\.com/
^https?://journals\.sagepub\.com/
^https?://www\.tandfonline\.com/
^https?://www\.economist\.com/
^https?://www\.nytimes\.com/

# Avi Wigderson's pages at IAS answered 403; both confirmed to exist, 2026-11-03.
^https?://www\.math\.ias\.edu/

# These answered lychee 403 on some runs and not others; each page confirmed to exist,
# 2026-11-03: Emily Riehl's book page, books.com.tw, a Medium post, Diane Poole Heller's
# book page, JMM 2021, and the Shaevitz Lab conference page.
^https?://math\.jhu\.edu/~eriehl/
^https?://www\.books\.com\.tw/
^https?://[a-z0-9-]+\.medium\.com/
^https?://traumasolutions\.com/
^https?://www\.jointmathematicsmeetings\.org/
^https?://shaevitzlab\.princeton\.edu/

# OpenReview answers 403 to automated requests. The NeurIPS 2026 paper link was given by the
# owner on 2026-11-02.
^https?://openreview\.net/
